## B. Method rules

| # | Requirement | Status | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| 19 | Write the edge down before any backtest | Met | `HYPOTHESIS.md`, commit `{{prereg.hyp.commit}}` ({{prereg.hyp.time}}), contains only the hypothesis; the commit time is authoritative |
| 20 | Commit the hypothesis before the first backtest | Met | Same commit; Appendix {{app:Records}} ("Pre-registration", "Deviations") gives the trail and `git log` count |
| 21 | Template: universe, behaviour, horizon, counterparty, persistence, prediction, falsifier | Met | §{{ref:sec:hyp}}, H6 box (all seven fields plus the trail) |
| 22 | Any liquid, publicly traded market | Team | Polymarket is a public order book with {{univ.volume}} traded in our universe and free tick data (§{{ref:sec:data}}). Prediction markets are not among the page's example asset classes; confirm with the organizers |
| 23 | Sponsor data optional; free public data allowed | Met | Public Polymarket and Kalshi APIs, Ken French, OpenTTGames, TrackNet |
| 24 | Holdout = most recent 20% or 2 years, whichever is shorter | Met (disclosed) | Last 20% of matches by start time (`src/tape.py`): {{univ.oos}} matches from {{univ.oosstart}}, {{univ.oos_vol}} of volume, {{univ.oos_time}} of calendar time; §{{ref:sec:data}} |
| 25 | Set the holdout aside early and don't look | Met | Split coded before any result; everything frozen before the single v1 open (`results/oos_peeks.log` line 1) |
| 26 | Evaluate the holdout once, at the end | Partly met | Opened once, blind, for v1 (Table {{ref:tab:A-all}}: {{v1.oos.usd}}). v2 and the CV simulation were designed after that, so their held-out numbers are labelled "burned (non-blind)" (abstract, §{{ref:sec:data}}, Table {{ref:tab:head}}). Clean tests: the blind unseen-market tests and the CV v3 rule's blind test (all fail, Table {{ref:tab:A-all}}). {{meta:fwd_label}}: {{fwd}} |
| 27 | Report the OOS result good or bad; report every peek in the note | Met | v1's loss, the blind-test fails and the doubled-cost loss are reported (Tables {{ref:tab:head}} and {{ref:tab:A-all}}); §{{ref:sec:results}} and Appendix {{app:Records}} ("Reads of held-out data") count the {{peeks.n}} reads of held-out data by class, including the lines logged after their run; `results/paper/peeks.json` lists every line |
| 28 | Walk-forward tuning inside IS, with a purge gap | Met (disclosed) | §{{ref:sec:method}} "Validation": monthly walk-forward inside IS; wallets qualify on past months only |
| 29 | Lag every signal; trade next; point-in-time data | Met (disclosed) | §{{ref:sec:method}}: wallets qualify on past months only; fills at the fast tier's own prints are labelled "the opportunity at their speed, not our execution"; §{{ref:sec:summary}}: the onset look-ahead found and fixed (D9), the V = 0 identity, the copier stress; copying 3 s later loses (Fig. {{ref:fig:edge}}a) |
| 30 | Cost in bps per trade, justified | Met | §{{ref:sec:method}} "Costs": fee = r·q·(1−q) per share = 10,000·r·(1−q) bps of notional, r = {{fee.rate}}; worked example in Calculation {{calc:Taker fee}}; fees paid {{v2.is.fee_bps}} / {{v2.oos.fee_bps}} bps of notional for v2 and {{cv.fee_bps.range}} bps for the CV trader (`results/tier0/cost_turnover.json`); spreads paid as traded |
| 31 | Show costs doubled; say so if the edge disappears | Met | Table {{ref:tab:head}} and Table {{ref:tab:A-all}} rows (½ and 1 tick worse entry, fees ×2, all costs ×2); §{{ref:sec:results}} and the abstract say the OOS edge turns negative when fees double (v2 {{v2.oos.fx2.c}}¢; every CV cell OOS, best {{cv.fx2.oos.best}} a day) |
| 32 | Survivorship, corporate actions and missing data explained in the note | Met | §{{ref:sec:data}} "Data problems": point-in-time universe ({{data.res5050.n}} 50/50 settlements, {{data.walk}} never started, {{data.retired}} retirements, all kept), volume-filter survivorship checked by the blind test on {{u2.markets}} smaller markets, {{data.offsetcap}} possibly truncated tapes, {{data.nofee}} no-fee matches, tape stamps lag {{data.blocklag}} s, gaps never filled from later prints, the 3 s to 1 s hold regime change |
| 33 | Guard against p-hacking: variants, plateau, deflated Sharpe | Met | §{{ref:sec:summary}} "Our Sharpe ratios are above 3" (the D9 bug fix: {{v2.onset.is.sr}} → {{v2.is.sr}}); PSR, MinTRL and the haircut over {{var.total}} variants (§{{ref:sec:results}}); deflated Sharpe at {{rig.N3386}} trials (Table {{ref:tab:head}}); variant tally in Appendix {{app:Records}}; PBO and bootstrap in Table {{ref:tab:A-all}} (verdict: luck not ruled out OOS); formulas and worked examples in Calculations {{calc:Probabilistic Sharpe}}–{{calc:Stationary block bootstrap}}; plateau in §{{ref:sec:results}}: all {{plat.sizing.pos}} sizing rules have IS per-share CIs above zero (Sharpe {{plat.sizing.sr}}), PBO {{plat.pbo}} across block choices, and the latency curve never rises by more than {{plat.lat.rise}} a day across {{plat.lat.n}} delays |
| 34 | Few parameters, simple rules with an economic reason | Met | §{{ref:sec:method}}: the v2 rules (detector, past-month qualification, sizing, caps, hold), each with its reason; Table {{ref:tab:A-all}} |
| 35 | Max DD, skew and worst month next to Sharpe; explain Sharpe > 3 | Met | Table {{ref:tab:head}}: return, volatility, Sharpe, max DD, turnover and fees ×2 for every book whose Sharpe is printed, IS and OOS (v2 skew and worst month in its notes); equity curves in Figs. {{ref:fig:edge}}b and {{ref:fig:firm}}a; §{{ref:sec:summary}} "Our Sharpe ratios are above 3"; Table {{ref:tab:head}} notes: the CV Sharpe ranks a simulation over trades selected on outcomes |
| 36 | Break results down by year or regime | Met | Fig. {{ref:fig:edge}} (by month), Fig. {{ref:fig:regime}} (fee and hold regimes) |
| 37 | Cite libraries and research; say what is new | Met | §{{ref:sec:method}} "The fast tier and v2" (copying is not new; what we add); References |
| 38 | AI tools allowed; the team answers for every line | Team | Disclosed in README and Devpost; every member must be able to explain the code and paper (`docs/QA_PREP.md`) |
| 39 | Any language | Info | Python |
| 40 | Check simple explanations; regress on known factors | Met | §{{ref:sec:risk}}: Fama–French + momentum α t = {{fac.alpha_t}}, max factor \|t\| {{fac.max_t}}; Table {{ref:tab:A-all}} (factor row); Calculation {{calc:Factor regression}} |
| 41 | Size by ADV; capacity in dollars; costs double | Met | §{{ref:sec:liq}}: v2 trades {{v2.is.notional_day}} a day, {{v2.is.share_vol}} of match volume; its OOS CI excludes zero only up to 1× size ({{cap.1x.oos.capital}}); the CV book has no capacity at the pre-registered lag; post hoc its Sharpe halves at {{capcv.half.oos}} (OOS) / {{capcv.half.is}} (IS) of capital, {{capcv.share_inplay}} of in-play volume ({{capcv.share_fast}} of the fast tier's 0–3 s volume); fixed-cost break-even and the most it can pay for data; Figs. {{ref:fig:capacity}} and {{ref:fig:cap}}; a price-impact model from {{liq.orders.fit}} IS taker orders and the live book ({{liq.M}}× cost just after a reprice; v2's 1× OOS {{liq.v2.1x.oos.central}} a day instead of {{liq.v2.1x.oos.none}}); doubled costs in Table {{ref:tab:head}} |
| 42 | Limits, de-risking rules, tail and regime | Met | §{{ref:sec:risk}}: limits and kill switches in code (`engine/risk/limits.py`), the net cap limits a match's open position to {{risk.maxloss}}, not its loss (v2 buys both tokens in {{risk.pm.twosided.is}} of matches; worst match {{risk.pm.worst.is}} IS, {{risk.pm.worst.oos}} OOS); only the backtest's $3,000 gross cap per match bounds a match ({{risk.pm.bound}}), and the live engine lacks it; a pre-registered per-wallet cap ({{wcap.W}} a day, backtest only) run once on the burned OOS ({{wcap.oos.c}}¢ {{wcap.oos.ci}}, non-blind; a loss limit, not a fix for concentration); de-risking rules set in advance; CV model risk (wrong calls, confidence gate, phantom calls, the rally gate, replayed on the engine's held-out call log (removes {{gate.out.removed}} of {{gate.out.total}} calls on unlabelled balls, keeps {{gate.correct.kept}} of {{gate.correct.total}} correct calls; not yet safe to trade)); tail, settlement (UMA), US access, legal; factors |
| 43 | Keep and report failures | Met | Abstract and §{{ref:sec:results}} (every blind test of a tradable book failed; doubled fees erase both books OOS; the fresh holdout's pre-registered reading lost); Table {{ref:tab:A-all}} (everything we tested, with the ex-ante replay rows and the forward-test row); Fig. {{ref:fig:replay}} (ex-ante replay); `DEVIATIONS.md` and `research/v2/tier0/DEVIATIONS.md` (rule changes after a look, counted in "What failed" and Appendix {{app:Records}}) |
| 44 | No funded accounts or real trading | Met | Read-only code; the engine is paper-only; no order was ever sent (`results/e2e/summary.json::counts.orders_sent` = {{e2e.sent}}) |
| 45 | Respect third-party licences and terms | Partly met | README "Data, sources and licences": TrackNet code and weights carry no licence and are used unmodified, not redistributed; ESPN/WTA terms were not reviewed (only derived timings committed) |
| 46 | Judges may re-run against held-out data | Info | `python scripts/forward_test.py --start ... --end ...` runs v2 on any window |

